🏢 Project Brief: Enterprise Financial & Expense Control Center
1. Executive Summary
The Enterprise Financial & Expense Control Center is a production-grade, multi-tenant expense management and corporate auditing system. It bridges the gap between lightweight expense loggers and monolithic enterprise resource planning (ERP) suites. Built with a decoupled architecture (FastAPI backend and Streamlit frontend), the application provides secure role-based access control (RBAC), departmental budget tracking, automated duplicate prevention, visual analytics, and professional PDF/CSV statement generation.

2. Core Architecture & Tech Stack
Backend Framework: FastAPI (Python) for high-performance RESTful API endpoints and data validation via Pydantic.

Frontend Interface: Streamlit styled with modern corporate UI components, interactive layout tabs, and responsive Plotly visualizations.

Database & Persistence: SQLite with robust relational integrity (enforcing unique constraint checks and multi-tenant partitioning).

Reporting & Compliance Engine: ReportLab for automated generation of publication-ready, formal corporate PDF audit reports.

3. Key Enterprise Features & Workflow
A. Multi-Tenant Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)
Employee Portal: Standard users log in with their corporate ID to submit expense claims, view their personal submission history, track approval statuses, and monitor their individual spend metrics.

Admin Portal: Administrators authenticate via a secure password-protected gateway (CorporateAdmin2026!). Admins gain global visibility across all employee submissions, access comparative budget analytics, and manage organization-wide cost centers.

B. Strict Data Integrity & Fraud Prevention
Unique Receipt Enforcement: The database schema enforces a unique constraint (UNIQUE) on receipt/invoice reference numbers (receipt_ref). The system instantly intercepts duplicate submissions and rejects them with clean HTTP 400 error validations.

Lifecycle Status Workflows: Every expense follows a controlled lifecycle—starting as Pending, and transitioning to Approved or Rejected through administrative review.

C. Departmental Budget Guardrails & Analytics
Cost Center Categorization: Expenses are categorized into professional business sectors (e.g., Travel & Conveyance, Client Entertainment, Software & Cloud, Office Supplies, Training & Upskilling).

Budget vs. Actual Comparison (Admin Only): Administrators can set monthly departmental thresholds and visualize real-time comparison metrics (Allocated Budget vs. Actual Spend) through grouped bar charts and automated progress monitors that flag budget breaches.

D. Audit Trail & Professional Reporting
Interactive Review Console: Admins can review claims, execute status overrides, append official reviewer comments/justifications, and modify claim parameters directly from the interface.

Export Capabilities: Generates real-time downloadable CSV audit spreadsheets as well as structured, formatted PDF expense statements.

4. How the System Works (Data Flow)
Submission: An employee fills out the expense form (vendor name, amount, category, payment channel, receipt reference ID, and business purpose).

Validation: FastAPI validates the payload against data models and checks SQLite to ensure the receipt reference doesn't already exist.

Storage & Review: The record is saved with a Pending status. The Admin views the item in the global audit dashboard, inspects justifications, and executes an Approve or Reject decision with comments.

Analytics & Reporting: Plotly aggregates the processed data into interactive charts, while ReportLab compiles authorized records into formal PDF statements for accounting handoff.







